=== 1. IFS= keeps the line, the last name keeps the raw rest
[  a  b  ]
[a b c][]
[b:c]
[b]
[b::]
[b]
[a][b  c]
[k][v=w]
3 [] [b]
=== 2. REPLY and backslashes
[ a  b  c  ]
[x y][z]
[xy][z]
[a:b][c]
[x\][y z]
=== 3. EOF clears the variables and fails
rc=1 [last]
rc=1 []
n=2
=== 4. -n / -N / -d
[a]
[x][]
[ab
c]
[x y][]
rc=0 [one]
rc=0 [a]
wbsh: read: x: invalid number
rc=1
=== 5. -u fd, -p, -s
[p][q]
[from three]
wbsh: read: 9: invalid file descriptor: Bad file descriptor
rc=1
[a b]
[secret]
=== 6. -t
t0 rc=0
timeout rc=142 []
t0 pipe rc=1
rc=1 [ab]
wbsh: read: abc: invalid timeout specification
rc=1
=== 7. bad options and names
wbsh: read: -z: invalid option
read: usage: read [-ers] [-a array] [-d delim] [-i text] [-n nchars] [-N nchars] [-p prompt] [-t timeout] [-u fd] [name ...]
rc=2
wbsh: read: `1x': not a valid identifier
rc=1
wbsh: read: -a: option requires an argument
read: usage: read [-ers] [-a array] [-d delim] [-i text] [-n nchars] [-N nchars] [-p prompt] [-t timeout] [-u fd] [name ...]
rc=2
